' TINY CROW'S NEST
' An original game by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio and
' Amy Bienvenu, 2026.
'
' The crows have nested in the farmer's crates, and the scarecrow has had
' enough: he flings pumpkins at them. Push the stick up and down to aim,
' hold the button to wind up the throw (the power swings up and down),
' let go to throw. Three pumpkins a stack (four for the last four); knock every crow out of its
' nest. Glass breaks and lets the pumpkin through; wood cracks or is
' shoved along, and a hard throw goes right through it; stone takes a hard throw. A block with nothing under
' it falls, unless it is held between two blocks or by a neighbour
' standing on something, so a good throw at the right block brings a
' whole stack down. A crow that falls, or that a block falls on, flies off.
'
' How the throw works: the starting speeds for every angle and power are
' worked out once (phys.py); in flight the pumpkin only adds its speeds
' and gravity, in 1/256 pixels.
'
' House rules kept: joystick only; text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22;
' tiles at 128 and up; a title tune that plays once (Amy's play song ...
' once); a credits page; the frame loop is protected from the NMI and
' every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a wait.

